cipline\" is a wide designation and therefore seems, at first impression, to indicate that the Assembly is obliged to commit…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md"},{"id":"bco:39-1--case:cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md:occ-ddd06814b970","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":489},"excerpt":"another” of the “modes of review\" (BCO 39-1), just like one city may have","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga51_2024__2023-04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["Sabbath observance","Super Bowl party","review and control","session records review","SJC jurisdiction","exception of substance","Westminster Confession 21:8","WLC 117","WLC 118","BCO 40-2","BCO 40-3","non-justiciability","adjacent courts","RAO Chapter 16"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2023-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Biese and others complained that Tennessee Valley Presbytery erred by approving Redeemer Church session minutes without exception—minutes noting a youth Super Bowl party—and by denying their complaint seeking a Sabbath exception. The SJC denied the complaint: because Presbytery gave no reasons for its actions, the record was insufficient to find it erred in interpreting the Constitution. A concurrence said the denial did not decide the Sabbath merits; a dissent would have held the complaint judicially out of order for lack of SJC jurisdiction over presbytery record review."}},{"id":"bco:39-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Harrell et al. v. Covenant Presbytery","year":2023,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-1--case:cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md:occ-fd268cd10456","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":508},"excerpt":"discretion and judgment\" per BCO 39-1.3. In evaluating such matters, the","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga50_2023__2022-07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["indictment specificity","sufficiency of indictment","BCO 32-5 times places circumstances","mission church polity","congregational right to select minister","organizing pastor election","fifth commandment","ninth commandment","disqualification of judges","standard of review in appeals","provisional Session authority","particularization of mission church","BCO 31-2 investigation","due process","mission church","particularization","congregational rights","minister selection","witnesses as judges","contumacy","location of trial","reference to presbytery","membership vows","slander","organizing pastor"],"standard_of_review":"factual_findings","review_standards":["factual_findings"],"case_numbers":["2022-7"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC sustained an appeal by seven members of a 38-member mission church who were convicted by their temporary Session of opposing the organizing minister's expected election as pastor. Reversing the Presbytery's affirmance and the guilty verdicts underlying indefinite suspensions, the SJC held the indictments fatally lacked BCO 32-5 specificity; Presbytery used the wrong standard of review; the Session had no authority to control pastoral selection; and no Fifth or Ninth Commandment offense was proved. Challenges to witness-judges, venue, and refusal to refer were rejected."}},{"id":"bco:39-1--case:cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"PCA v. Gulfstream","year":2011,"disposition":"administrative","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-1--case:cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.md:occ-66a0a0c67f68","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":133},"excerpt":"- **a.** A pending matter is a matter with respect to which process (BCO 31-2, ¶2) has commenced or which has been filed under the Rules of Discipline with the appropriate court. A matter continues to be pending through any appellate process. (BCO 39-1).","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2010-18_2010-19_2010-20_2010-21_2010-22_2010-23.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["review of presbytery records","exceptions of substance","RAO 16-10(c)"],"case_numbers":["2010-23"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Pacific Presbytery was cited and appeared before the SJC regarding exceptions of substance found in its records; the SJC accepted the presbytery's response as acceptable, pending certification that the response was approved by the presbytery."}}],"history":[]}
